$DATUM 7789-23-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: S-alkylation of thiols into corresponding
thioethers by KF/Al2O3 under solvent-free reaction conditions assisted by
microwave irradiation (Method B) A suitable quantity of alkyl halides
(1.5 mmol) and KF/Al2O3 (0.6 g) was added to a specific test tube (h = 9
cm, d = 1.5 cm) containing the thiol (1.5 mmol). The test tube was placed
into a Discover CEM microwave oven. For each of the thiols, an
irradiation program was fixed to operate at power of oven (4 W), reaction
temperature (50°C) and reaction time (minutes), see Table 1. After
cooling, the reaction mixture was extracted with dichloromethane (4 × 15
mL). The combined extracts were filtered, washed with water until
neutral, and then dried by anhydrous Na2SO4. After removal of the solvent
by rotary evaporation, the remaining crude product was analyzed by GC/MS
and NMR spectroscopy. 2-Butylthio-4,5-dihydrothiazole (Entry 9, Table 1).
1H NMR (CDCl3): δH = 4.20 (t, J = 7.5Hz, 2H), 3.36 (t, J = 8.0Hz, 2H),
3.09 (t, J = 7.5Hz, 2H), 1.66 (quintet, J = 7.5Hz, 2H), 1.41 (sextet, J =
7.5Hz, 2H), 0.91 (t, J = 7.5Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δC = 166.34, 64.10,
35.19, 32.52, 31.23, 21.82, 13.52. MS (ESI+): m/z = 176.0537 ([M]+, 98%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry-catalyst, microwave irradiation (4W),
solid-supported catalyst, potassium fluoride supported on alumina used as
a catalyst, no solvent, alternative reaction conditions shown, catalyst
prepared and used, recyclable catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Benign and efficient preparation of thioethers by solvent-free
S-alkylation of thiols with alkyl halides catalyzed by potassium fluoride
on alumina
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nguyen, Kha Ngoc; Duus, Fritz; Luu, Thi Xuan Thi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Sulfur Chemistry (2016), 37(3), 349-360

